---
title: Pan Fried Tofu with Caramelised Sauce
servings: 4
course: Started
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

= Drain Tofu =

Drain the @tofu{570%g}(2 blocks) and wrap in three layers of kitchen paper. Put a large plate or chopping board on top as a weight. Leave for ~{30%minutes} to allow time for the excess liquid to be absorbed by the paper. 

= Prepare Marinade =

Chop the @spring onions{4} finely. Mix with the @sake{4%tbsp}, @soy sauce{4%tbsp}, and @mirin{4%tbsp} in a shallow bowl. Leave for 15 minutes

= Fry Garlic Chips =

Slice the @garlic{4%cloves} very thinly to make garlic chips. Heat the @vegetable oil{2%tsp} in a frying pan and fry the garlic for a few moments until golden. Turn the chips frequently to prevent sticking and burning. Scoop them out onto kitchen paper. Reserve the oil in the pan.

= Marinade Tofu =

Unwrap the tofu and cut into 2 cm cubes. Soak in the marinade for about ~{15%minutes}.

= Fry and Serve Tofu =

Take out the tofu and wipe off the excess marinade with kitchen paper. Reserve the marinade.

Reheat the oil in the frying pan and add one piece of @butter{50%g}(cut into 5 equal pieces). When the oil starts sizzling, reduce the heat to medium and add the pieces of tofu one by one. Cook in one layer, if possible.

Cover and cook until the edge of the tofu is browned and quite firm, approximately 5-8 minutes on each side. (If the edges burn but the centre is pale, reduce the heat.)

Pour the marinade into the pan. Cook for 2 minutes, or until the spring onion is very soft. Remove the tofu and arrange on each serving plate. Pour the thickened marinade and spring onion mixture over the tofu and top with a piece of butter. Sprinkle with the garlic chips and garnish with @watercress. Serve hot.